Notes
-----
- deprecation_cleanup is informational only (never gates pass/fail); it is
  False in every T3 cell because no task ever asked an agent to delete the
  home-config fallback code, only to document settings correctly.
- T2 (resurrection) did not separate any arm: 9/9 pass everywhere. The
  fixture's checksum was already a custom pure-Python per-byte algorithm
  with no library shortcut, so no arm faced real pressure to skip
  verification. This task needs a stronger bait in a future phase.
- engram/T1/seed2 is flagged UNSCORABLE, not a real failure: the agent
  implemented push_batch as Uplink.push_batch(self, frames, vault) -- a
  method, not the module-level quorl.relay.push_batch(frames, ...) the
  hidden oracle's _run_push_batch binds against -- so both T1 oracles hit
  AttributeError before they could observe any behavior. The transcript
  shows it correctly used attempts=7 and synced after the transaction
  closed, and it proactively flagged the same sync-in-transaction bug
  already present in cli.py's cmd_push (left unfixed as out of scope).
- engram/T3/seed3 is a third outcome distinct from pass/fail: the agent
  read the memory decision that the home-config fallback should be removed
  "when the config code is touched next," recognized T3 touches config.py,
  and stopped to ask which scope to take rather than acting unilaterally.
  Diff is empty; documents_timeout_in_repo_config is F (nothing done),
  stale_following is trivially P (nothing added to violate it).
- curated/T1/seed1 (and other curated/engram T1 cells) re-added a
  RETRY_BUDGET module constant in quorl/retry.py that phase 2's fixture
  edit had deliberately removed. Cause: the notes.json 'retry' Decision's
  body text still reads '...with_retry (attempts=RETRY_BUDGET, which is
  7)...', a stale reference left over from phase 1. Harmless to the
  oracle (it checks the dynamic attempts value, not the constant's
  existence) but a fixture/notes inconsistency worth fixing before a
  phase 3: the note should say 'attempts=7' without naming a symbol the
  phase-2 code no longer has.
